    {
      "text": "one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass from the law, Matt. 5:18 (3 Ne. 12:18). there is none good but one, that is, God, Matt. 19:17. one fold, and one shepherd, John 10:16. I and my Father are one, John 10:30. that they may be one, as we are, John 17:11 (17:22). they all may be one … that they also may be one in us, John 17:21. continued with one accord in prayer, Acts 1:14 (15:25). them that believed were of one heart and of one soul, Acts 4:32. hath made of one blood all nations of men, Acts 17:26. it is one God, which shall justify, Rom. 3:30. gift by grace, which is by one man, Jesus Christ, Rom. 5:15. So we, being many, are one body in Christ, Rom. 12:5. he that is joined unto the Lord is one spirit, 1 Cor. 6:17. there is but one God … and one Lord Jesus Christ, 1 Cor. 8:6. be of one mind, 2 Cor. 13:11 (1 Pet. 3:8). neither male nor female … all one in Christ, Gal. 3:28. to make in himself of twain one new man, Eph. 2:15. One Lord, one faith, one baptism, Eph. 4:5. stand fast in one spirit, with one mind, Philip. 1:27. there is one God, and one mediator, 1 Tim. 2:5. he that sanctifieth and they who are sanctified are all of one, Heb. 2:11. the Father, the Word, and the Holy Ghost: and these three are one, 1 Jn. 5:7 (2 Ne. 31:21; Alma 11:44; 3 Ne. 11:36; D&C 20:28).",
